/// FINDING (v-compiler-ml, 2026-07-16) — `String.to-bytes` of a RUNTIME string DECLINES ("String.to-bytes
/// of a runtime string is not yet computed (constant strings only)"), the INVERSE of the now-FIXED
/// `String.from-bytes` (which reads runtime bytes fine). This is the encoder-side blocker to completing the
/// compiler-ml codec's Name/Str CONTENT round-trip.
///
/// CONTEXT: `String.from-bytes(runtime-bytes)` now works (a sibling fixed it — decode.cdz could finally
/// read a Name's UTF-8 content). I went to complete the round-trip by having encode.cdz write the name
/// bytes via `String.to-bytes(n)` — but `String.to-bytes` still only const-folds; a name string threaded
/// through the recursive `encode` (so genuinely runtime) declines. So the codec's Name/Str content STILL
/// can't round-trip — now blocked on the OTHER half.
///
/// REPRO (declines at `cdz compile`; `cdz check` is clean):
///   type Ast = Int(Int64) | Name(String) | List(List(Ast))
///   def str-payload(s) = Bytes.concat(b1(String.byte-len(s)), String.to-bytes(s))
///   def encode(node) = match node { … Name(n) => Bytes.concat(b1(2), str-payload(n)) … List(kids) => … enclist … }
///   encode(Ast.Name("foo"))  →  "String.to-bytes of a runtime string is not yet computed"
///
/// DISCRIMINATORS (verified):
///   • `String.to-bytes("hi")` on a plain CONSTANT folds fine (→ 2 bytes).
///   • `String.to-bytes(s)` where s is a param, called with a literal that const-propagates, folds.
///   • But inside a RECURSIVE encoder (encode/enclist mutual recursion) the Name payload is genuinely
///     runtime and `String.to-bytes(n)` DECLINES — the shape any real serializer takes.
///
/// FIX: give `String.to-bytes` a runtime lowering (a String is a heap UTF-8 rope; to-bytes should be ~the
/// identity to a Bytes handle, the mirror of the runtime `String.from-bytes` that already landed). This
/// unblocks the compiler-ml codec (encode.cdz) to serialize Name/Str content, completing the Ast↔bytes
/// round-trip that has been content-less (placeholder "") since iteration 1.
def b1(x: Int64) = Bytes.of([UInt8.wrap(x)])
type Ast = Int(Int64) | Name(String) | List(List(Ast))
def str-payload(s: String) = Bytes.concat(b1(String.byte-len(s)), String.to-bytes(s))
def encode(node: Ast) = match node with
  | Ast.Int(v) => Bytes.concat(b1(0), b1(v))
  | Ast.Name(n) => Bytes.concat(b1(2), str-payload(n))
  | Ast.List(kids) => Bytes.concat(Bytes.concat(b1(3), b1(List.len(kids))), enclist(kids))
def enclist(xs: List(Ast)) = match xs with | [] => Bytes.of([]) | [h, .. t] => Bytes.concat(encode(h), enclist(t))
def run() = Bytes.len(encode(Ast.Name("foo")))
export { run }
